msgid "Actual weight: kilograms and pounds"
msgstr "Actual weight: kilograms and pounds"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1715
msgid "Adaptive cruise control and speed-limit assist features depend on map data units. If the car was configured for another market, verify the shown limit against roadside signs once, especially after firmware or language changes."
msgstr "Adaptive cruise control and speed-limit assist features depend on map data units. If the car was configured for another market, verify the shown limit against roadside signs once, especially after firmware or language changes."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:154
msgid "Adding 273.15 directly to Fahrenheit skips the scale change and produces nonsense. Rankine (°R) is the Fahrenheit-sized absolute scale; do not label Rankine values as Kelvin. Oven setpoints in °F are not absolute temperatures for gas-law homework."
msgstr "Adding 273.15 directly to Fahrenheit skips the scale change and produces nonsense. Rankine (°R) is the Fahrenheit-sized absolute scale; do not label Rankine values as Kelvin. Oven setpoints in °F are not absolute temperatures for gas-law homework."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:384
msgid "Adding 50% (×1.5) understates true km/h. Aircraft indicated airspeed in knots is not mph—convert knots separately. Treadmill mph to km/h is the same factor as road speed."
msgstr "Adding 50% (×1.5) understates true km/h. Aircraft indicated airspeed in knots is not mph—convert knots separately. Treadmill mph to km/h is the same factor as road speed."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:104
msgid "Adding leftover inches twice—once inside the feet field and again after converting—double-counts. Decimal feet (6.5 ft) become 78 inches, not 6 ft 5 in (which is 77 inches). Confirm whether the source already mixed feet and inches in one string."
msgstr "Adding leftover inches twice—once inside the feet field and again after converting—double-counts. Decimal feet (6.5 ft) become 78 inches, not 6 ft 5 in (which is 77 inches). Confirm whether the source already mixed feet and inches in one string."

