msgstr "Convert km/h to m/s for drag equations, ballistic apps, and lab write-ups that need SI base units. Divide km/h by 3.6. Engineering fluid notes and school physics prefer m/s."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:377
msgid "Convert km/h to mph for road speed limits, car dashboards, and running pace talk when traveling between metric and US/UK customary roads. Divide km/h by 1.609344. Rental cars and GPS unit settings drive this daily."
msgstr "Convert km/h to mph for road speed limits, car dashboards, and running pace talk when traveling between metric and US/UK customary roads. Divide km/h by 1.609344. Rental cars and GPS unit settings drive this daily."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:413
msgid "Convert knots to km/h for marine and aviation contexts when instruments show knots but coastal forecasts or metric pilots want km/h. One knot is one nautical mile per hour = 1.852 km/h exactly. Charts and AIS traffic use knots; phones often show km/h."
msgstr "Convert knots to km/h for marine and aviation contexts when instruments show knots but coastal forecasts or metric pilots want km/h. One knot is one nautical mile per hour = 1.852 km/h exactly. Charts and AIS traffic use knots; phones often show km/h."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2215
