msgid "Kilograms and pounds both describe mass (weight under ordinary gravity). A suitcase that tips a scale at 23 kg is the same object whether a US tag says about 50.7 lb. The physics does not change; the number and the unit do. Confusion starts when people treat the numbers as interchangeable, round too early, or mix stone, pounds, and kilograms on one form."
msgstr "Kilograms and pounds both describe mass (weight under ordinary gravity). A suitcase that tips a scale at 23 kg is the same object whether a US tag says about 50.7 lb. The physics does not change; the number and the unit do. Confusion starts when people treat the numbers as interchangeable, round too early, or mix stone, pounds, and kilograms on one form."

