msgstr "Many international economy limits sit at 23 kg (often marketed as 50 lb). That marketing round is slightly generous: 23 × 2.2046226218 ≈ 50.71 lb. If your home scale only shows pounds, do not pack to a flat 50 lb and assume you are safe—you may already be over. Convert the airline’s kilogram limit into pounds with a proper converter, then leave a buffer for scale disagreement between home and the check-in desk."

