#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1395
msgid "Write both °C and °F on a sticky note for family recipes you reuse. Dual labels prevent weekend arguments and burnt trays."
msgstr "Write both °C and °F on a sticky note for family recipes you reuse. Dual labels prevent weekend arguments and burnt trays."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:607
msgid "Write m² and m³ with clear superscripts or ASCII m^2 and m^3 in plain text. A bare m next to a number that meant cubic metres will be misread later."
msgstr "Write m² and m³ with clear superscripts or ASCII m^2 and m^3 in plain text. A bare m next to a number that meant cubic metres will be misread later."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1335
msgid "Write the unit on every sketch dimension. A bare “12 × 15” is ambiguous across borders. Prefer “12 ft × 15 ft” or “3.66 m × 4.57 m”."
msgstr "Write the unit on every sketch dimension. A bare “12 × 15” is ambiguous across borders. Prefer “12 ft × 15 ft” or “3.66 m × 4.57 m”."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:466
msgid "Write units on every line of a calculation. Prefix errors hide in bare numbers. Dimensional analysis still works when prefixes are treated as part of the unit token."
msgstr "Write units on every line of a calculation. Prefix errors hide in bare numbers. Dimensional analysis still works when prefixes are treated as part of the unit token."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2003
msgid "Write units on the sketch: “3.20 m × 4.10 m” or “10 ft 6 in × 13 ft 5 in.” Bare numbers cause expensive callbacks."
msgstr "Write units on the sketch: “3.20 m × 4.10 m” or “10 ft 6 in × 13 ft 5 in.” Bare numbers cause expensive callbacks."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:248
msgid "Writing “mL” on a value still in litres by habit (1 L ≠ 1 mL). Baby formula and concentrate ratios break if you convert volume but keep the powder mass wrong. Carbonated beverage “litres” on bottles are liquid volume, not dissolved-gas volume."
msgstr "Writing “mL” on a value still in litres by habit (1 L ≠ 1 mL). Baby formula and concentrate ratios break if you convert volume but keep the powder mass wrong. Carbonated beverage “litres” on bottles are liquid volume, not dissolved-gas volume."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:358
msgid "Writing 1.5 kg as 1.5 g on a scale that reads grams underdoses by 1,000×. Shipping dimensional weight in kg is unrelated to converting product mass to grams—keep those workflows separate. Jewelry grams are mass; carats are different."
msgstr "Writing 1.5 kg as 1.5 g on a scale that reads grams underdoses by 1,000×. Shipping dimensional weight in kg is unrelated to converting product mass to grams—keep those workflows separate. Jewelry grams are mass; carats are different."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:458
msgid "Writing 90 minutes as 1.90 hours is wrong—90/60 = 1.5 h. Movie runtimes in minutes convert cleanly; including trailers is a content choice, not a unit issue. Keep overtime rules (e.g. round to next 15 min) separate from pure conversion."
msgstr "Writing 90 minutes as 1.90 hours is wrong—90/60 = 1.5 h. Movie runtimes in minutes convert cleanly; including trailers is a content choice, not a unit issue. Keep overtime rules (e.g. round to next 15 min) separate from pure conversion."

